WEBVTT

00:11:28.411 --> 00:11:31.478
Well, the nice thing is,
it doesn't require a huge shift.

00:11:31.977 --> 00:11:34.523
Small things can make a big difference.

00:11:35.108 --> 00:11:37.766
I found that thanking people,

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.256
sharing credit,

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.012
listening attentively,

00:11:41.663 --> 00:11:44.092
humbly asking questions,

00:11:44.116 --> 00:11:46.831
acknowledging others and smiling

00:11:46.855 --> 00:11:48.243
has an impact.

00:11:49.497 --> 00:11:53.232
Patrick Quinlan, former CEO
of Ochsner Health [System],

00:11:53.256 --> 00:11:56.113
told me about the effects
of their 10-5 way,

00:11:56.137 --> 00:11:58.395
where if you're within 10 feet of someone,

00:11:58.419 --> 00:12:01.069
you make eye contact and smile,